<article class="env-lemma" id="0859">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0859">Lemma <span data-tag="0859">70.14.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $T \subset |X|$ be a closed subset and let $U \subset X$ be the open subspace such that $T \amalg |U| = |X|$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Consider the sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules $\mathcal{F}'$ which associates to every object $\varphi : W \to X$ of $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ the module </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F}'(W) = \{ s \in \mathcal{F}(W) \mid \text{the support of }s\text{ is contained in }|\varphi |^{-1}(T)\}   \]
</div>
  <p> If $U \to X$ is quasi-compact, then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for $W$ affine there exist a finitely generated ideal $I \subset \mathcal{O}_ X(W)$ such that $|\varphi |^{-1}(T) = V(I)$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for $W$ and $I$ as in (1) we have $\mathcal{F}'(W) = \{ x \in \mathcal{F}(W) \mid I^ nx = 0 \text{ for some } n\} $, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}'$ is a quasi-coherent sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear that the rule defining $\mathcal{F}'$ gives a subsheaf of $\mathcal{F}$. Hence we may work étale locally on $X$ to verify the other statements. Thus the lemma reduces to the case of schemes which is Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZP" data-tag="07ZP">28.25.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>